# Three-Dot Hover

Every three-dot control (⋮ / ⋯) that owns a menu **opens that popover on hover**.
The user does not tap or click first. Touch and keyboard still toggle on tap /
Enter.

## What this means on the surface

- Hover the ⋮ → the menu appears, anchored above or to the right of the icon
  (never directly below — see the popover conventions rule).
- Move onto the menu → it stays open.
- Leave both the icon and the menu → it closes.
- Tap on a touch device, or press Enter while focused → the same menu toggles,
  same as before.

## How it is wired

Shared module: `js/kebab-hover.js`, injected from `js/agent-menu.js` on every
page that renders the WISE nav. It clicks the existing trigger so each
surface’s own open handler still runs. Do not reimplement hover-open per page.

Row ⋮ buttons are excluded from the icon-label tooltip (`js/lir-tooltip.js`) —
the menu **is** the hover result, not an “Actions” card.

## Rules for the agent

- Never leave a new three-dot without a popover. If the control is a ⋮, hovering
  it must open a menu.
- Do not make a three-dot menu click-only. Hover is the default on pointer
  devices.
- Do not show a separate “Actions” / “More options” tooltip on a ⋮ that already
  opens a menu.
- Touch must still work: no hover, tap toggles.
